    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "366f00b6_a7d4d309",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 588,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T04:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does it mean for mMatchWifiNetworkKeys to contain null ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 588,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 588,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "e7b6657b766634f583a8e019686474577e06a636",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e27a6275_2fe0a534",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 588,
      "author": {
        "id": 1385042
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-18T05:50:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we don\u0027t want to have null in the keys, however, we did not really restrict it in all constructors.\nSome removed constructors/buildTemplate* (such like `buildTemplateWifi(@Nullable String wifiNetworkKey,@Nullable String subscriberId)`) will use `wifiNetworkKey \u003d\u003d null ? new String[0] : new String[] {wifiNetworkKey}` to avoid mMatchWifiNetworkKeys to contain null.\n\nIf users use the Builder then [NetworkTemplate.Builder#setWifiNetworkKeys](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java;l\u003d817?q\u003dNetworkTemplate.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.) will throw IAE if there\u0027s a key is null.\n\nToday only the @hide [constructor](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java;l\u003d308?q\u003dNetworkTemplate.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:aosp-master%20file:.) could build a template with mMatchWifiNetworkKeys that contains null.",
      "parentUuid": "366f00b6_a7d4d309",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 588,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 588,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "e7b6657b766634f583a8e019686474577e06a636",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4723b2e1_4b8282d9",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 588,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-21T05:27:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So IIUC, we can make 100% sure it never happens by surveying all callers, and once we know no callers do this change the @hide constructor to throw in that case ? Can we just do that, and then simplify this code ?",
      "parentUuid": "e27a6275_2fe0a534",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 588,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 588,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "e7b6657b766634f583a8e019686474577e06a636",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5ced003_29802973",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 588,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-07T09:18:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To the question above: Yes but I\u0027m not sure we can say no caller do this anymore consider that they might invoke our hidden methods.\n\nWhat does it mean for mMatchWifiNetworkKeys to contain null ?\nThat means the caller may want to match wifi networks which uses null as their wifi key, which does not make any sense becasue all wifi should have a non-null wifi key.\nGiven that nulls are not never a valid input, and they should not match any given wifiNetworkKey. I think we can leave it as is for now, since it won\u0027t match any non-null wifiNetworkKey, and if wifiNetworkKey is null, we simply return true at l.585 if it is wildcard case.",
      "parentUuid": "4723b2e1_4b8282d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 588,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 588,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "e7b6657b766634f583a8e019686474577e06a636",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
